[{"id":3956083457,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7rzQsB","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nIn terms of UX, this seems fine but I think the Transform menu should be changed to be more consistent with the View menu. Currently, we rarely (if ever) use separators above sections of radio buttons in the editor.\r\n\r\nCurrent | Proposed\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"304\" height=\"82\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cef03699-af38-425a-a4ea-d46180e29171\" /> | <img width=\"304\" height=\"82\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c659088-a914-42d2-9a06-ae2b1909db7d\" />\r\n\r\nThere should also be tooltips for each option:\r\n\r\n- **Snap Vertex to Vertex:** \r\n  - Hold (shortcut key) to highlight a vertex on the currently selected node, then drag the mouse to move the node and snap it to neighboring nodes' vertices. For nodes that do not have a vertex-based representation, Snap Origin to Vertex is always used instead.\r\n- **Snap Origin to Vertex:**\r\n  - Hold (shortcut key) to highlight another node's vertex, then click to teleport the selected node to the highlighted vertex.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117380#pullrequestreview-3956083457","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117380","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-03-16T19:16:14Z"},{"id":3956700383,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7r1nTf","state":"COM